note right of DeviceFactory
  A42 replaces central subtype switches with
  DeviceRegistry-backed dispatch.
  Unregistered / unavailable sub-types still
  resolve as nullptr.
end note

note right of IPlcTagProvider
  A40 moves PLC tag-list capability out of IDevice.
  Only PLC-family devices expose digital/word tags now.
end note

note right of IPlcIoWriter
  Localization runtime uses this PLC-family capability
  for queued task output writes such as bTaskReady,
  bTaskFault, and nFaultCode.
end note

note right of VisionTcpipDeviceBase
  Shared TCP/IP protocol core (framing, heartbeat,
  pushRequest, runtime state / diagnostics). The
  software is always the heartbeat master.
  VisionTcpipDevice = TCP server (listen + accept);
  VisionTcpipClientDevice = TCP client (dial-out +
  reconnect). JSON persistence stays config-only.
end note

note bottom of RobotDevice
  Robot family exists, but vendor devices are
  minimum stubs and no RobotRunner is wired.
end note

note bottom of IsVirtualDevice
  R8 - a virtual device must never pass for a real one.
  Three markers (project-tree VIRT chip, device-panel
  banner, per-runtime-start log warning) all read this
  one predicate so they cannot disagree.
  There is deliberately no virtual Robot: nothing
  consumes one.
end note

note right of VirtualCameraDevice
  Sub-type token is "Virtual" in all three families
  (tokens are family-local). Enumerators cannot be:
  these are unscoped enums, so all three would collide
  in vc::device - hence VirtualCamera / VirtualPlc /
  VirtualVisionOutput.

  Calibration is SYNTHETIC: the homography is really
  fitted by calib::Calibrator, but the scene (flat,
  axis-aligned, at millimetresPerPixel) is asserted.
  millimetresPerPixel = 0 leaves it uncalibrated, and
  the runtime then refuses it exactly as it refuses a
  real uncalibrated camera.
end note

note right of VirtualPlcDevice
  IPlcTagProvider is what makes it usable:
  LocalizationSettingWidget clears both signal-map
  lists for a device implementing neither tag
  interface. Advertises M0..M<n-1> / D0..D<n-1>.
  Writes to invalid MC addresses are rejected, not
  merely accepted.

  Known gap (backlog #43): values cannot be injected
  IN, so a task reaches Ready and no further.
end note

